{"archetypes":[{"name":"branch-guard-logic","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The guards have subtle logic branches (state branch vs current branch, empty values, detached HEAD) that need independent correctness verification beyond the generic reviewer.","prompt_body":"Examine each branch-guard condition in ship-pr.sh run_bump_phase() and step2-implement.sh: verify the boolean logic covers all intended cases (main, master, mismatch, empty BRANCH_NAME, detached HEAD returning empty string). Check whether the OR conditions are correctly grouped and whether short-circuit evaluation could cause any guard to silently pass when it should fire. Confirm that emit_bailed and exit_stall are invoked with the correct arguments and that no code path allows the guarded logic to execute after a guard fires. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"resume-path-coverage","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan claims the bump guard fires on --resume-phase bump but does not add guards to run_rebase_rebump; verifying this boundary decision requires integration-level review.","prompt_body":"Trace all entry points into run_bump_phase() including --resume-phase invocations and any callers that bypass the normal flow to confirm the new guard is always reached before bump work begins. Verify that run_rebase_rebump truly operates on an already-validated branch and cannot be reached with BRANCH_NAME=main/master. Check whether skipping the guard in run_rebase_rebump creates a residual escape path. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
